# Advanced RAG workbench. Copy this file to .env and fill in ONE provider block.
#     cp .env.example .env
# Never commit .env. Model ids live here and in rag/settings.py only, never in a notebook.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOU DO NOT NEED A KEY TO START.
# Every lab in this course runs offline. Clone, install, and `pytest -q` goes green
# with this file untouched. Add a key when you want a hosted model to write the
# answers; the retrieval half never needs one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ===========================================================================
# THE THREE VARIABLES
# Every hosted provider in this course is reached by setting these three.
# The code never changes when the provider does.
# ===========================================================================
#   LLM_BASE_URL   where to send the request
#   LLM_API_KEY    who you are
#   LLM_MODEL      which model answers
#
# A fourth var picks the wire format, because not every vendor speaks the same one:
#   LLM_BACKEND=openai      OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions  (most vendors)
#   LLM_BACKEND=anthropic   Anthropic Messages /v1/messages      (Claude)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI
# Docs: https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference
# Pricing: https://openai.com/api/pricing/   (check it; prices move)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_BACKEND=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
#
# Drop-in alternatives, cheapest to most capable (verified against the models page
# 2026-09-01; confirm before you rely on any id, because vendors retire them):
#   gpt-5.6-luna    cost-optimised, high volume. Fine for every lab in this course
#   gpt-5.6-terra   balances intelligence and cost
#   gpt-5.6-sol     the flagship, for complex professional work


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC (Claude)
# Claude does NOT speak the OpenAI chat format on its native endpoint, so this
# block sets LLM_BACKEND=anthropic. That is the only difference; the workbench
# code is identical.
# Docs:    https://docs.anthropic.com/en/api/messages
# Models:  https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models
# Pricing: https://www.anthropic.com/pricing   (check it; prices move)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_BACKEND=anthropic
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
#
# Drop-in alternatives, cheapest to most capable. Use the id exactly as written,
# with no date suffix:
#   claude-haiku-4-5     fast and cheap, fine for every lab in this course
#   claude-sonnet-5      the balanced default for real work
#   claude-opus-5        the most capable
# Confirm the current list on the models page above before you rely on any id.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL: nothing leaves your machine
# This is the setup regulated teams actually ship, and it costs nothing.
# Install Ollama (https://ollama.com), then:  ollama pull qwen3:8b
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_BACKEND=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=ollama
# LLM_MODEL=qwen3:8b
#
# LM Studio is the same shape on a different port:
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
#
# Laptop-capable models: qwen3:8b, llama3.2:3b, llama3.2:1b, gemma3:4b, qwen2.5:3b, phi4-mini


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERY OTHER PROVIDER IS THE SAME THREE VARIABLES
# If it speaks the OpenAI chat format, it works here with no code change.
# Fill in the base URL and model from that vendor's own docs; this course does
# not track other vendors' ids, because they change faster than a video does.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Grok (xAI)      LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.x.ai/v1
# Google Gemini   LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
# Qwen            LLM_BASE_URL=https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
# Together        LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.together.xyz/v1
# Groq            LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#
# In each case: LLM_BACKEND=openai, plus your key and a model id from their docs.


# ===========================================================================
# EMBEDDINGS: a SECOND model, and a separate decision
# ===========================================================================
# RAG makes two model calls. One embeds, one writes. They do not have to come
# from the same vendor, and Anthropic does not serve embeddings at all, so a
# Claude setup still needs an embedder from somewhere else.
#
# The course default is a real local model. Free, no key, already installed with
# the requirements, and good enough for every lab here.
EMBED_MODEL=all-MiniLM-L6-v2
#
# Hosted alternative (needs LLM_API_KEY set to an OpenAI key):
# EMBED_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
#
# The teaching toy, used in exactly one lecture so you can read every number by
# hand. 64 dimensions, deterministic, keyless. Never use it for real retrieval:
# EMBED_MODEL=hash


# ===========================================================================
# HOW THE ANSWER IS PRODUCED
# ===========================================================================
# extractive  pull the answer span straight from the retrieved text (no key needed)
# generate    hand the retrieved text to the model above and let it write
RAGBENCH_GENERATE=extractive
